# MusterPoint AI Development Guidelines

## Project Overview
MusterPoint is a Warhammer 40K army list builder using Blazor WebAssembly (.NET 9) with a MongoDB backend. This file provides strict guidelines for AI-assisted development to maintain code quality and consistency.

---

## 1. CSS & Styling Framework

### Primary Framework: Bulma
- **Always use Bulma** (https://bulma.io/) as the primary CSS framework
- Bulma version: 1.0+
- Use Bulma components for all UI elements (buttons, forms, cards, etc.)
- Leverage Bulma's utility classes for spacing, sizing, and layout

### CSS Class-Based Only
- **NEVER use inline styles** (style attribute)
- **NEVER use <style> blocks** in Razor components
- **ALWAYS use CSS classes** referencing external stylesheets
- Store all component-specific styles in `.razor.css` files
- Store global styles in `/wwwroot/app.css`

### CSS Organization
```
MusterPoint/
??? wwwroot/
?   ??? app.css      # Global styles
??? Components/
    ??? MyComponent.razor.css      # Component-specific styles
```

### Example - CORRECT ?
```razor
@* MyComponent.razor *@
<div class="my-component">
    <h1 class="title is-3">Hello</h1>
    <button class="button is-primary">Click me</button>
</div>

@* MyComponent.razor.css *@
.my-component {
    padding: 2rem;
    background-color: #f5f5f5;
}

.my-component .title {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
```

### Example - WRONG ?
```razor
@* DON'T DO THIS *@
<div style="padding: 2rem; background-color: #f5f5f5;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Hello</h1>
    <button style="background-color: blue; color: white; padding: 0.5rem;">Click me</button>
</div>

<style>
    .my-component { padding: 2rem; }
</style>
```

