## 3. Clean Architecture

### Layered Structure
```
MusterPoint/
??? Controllers/    # API endpoints (thin layer)
??? Services/   # Business logic
??? Models/         # Domain entities
??? Data/            # Data access (repositories)
??? Components/        # UI components (Blazor)

MusterPoint.Client/
??? Pages/        # Blazor pages
??? Services/             # Client-side services
??? Models/ # Client DTOs/models
??? Components/           # Reusable Razor components
```

### Separation of Concerns
- **Controllers**: Route requests, delegate to services
- **Services**: Implement business logic, coordinate repositories
- **Repositories**: Data access only
- **Models**: Plain data carriers (entities, DTOs)
- **Components**: UI rendering only (no business logic)

### Data Flow
```
Client ? Controller ? Service ? Repository ? Database
         (routing)   (logic)    (data)
```

### Rules
1. **Never put business logic in controllers** - Controllers should only route and delegate
2. **Never put data access in services** - Services use repositories for data
3. **Never put business logic in components** - Components should call services
4. **Never reference controllers from services** - Services are independent
5. **Never put SQL/MongoDB queries in services** - Queries belong in repositories

