## 4. Blazor Component Guidelines

### Component Structure
```razor
@page "/path"
@using Namespace
@inject ServiceType ServiceName

<Component>
    <!-- Template HTML using Bulma classes only -->
</Component>

@code {
 // Properties
    private string? variable;
    
    // Lifecycle methods
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() { }
    
    // Event handlers
    private async Task HandleEvent() { }
}
```

### Rules for Components
- Use Bulma classes exclusively for styling
- Keep components as presentation layer only
- Call injected services for logic
- Always use proper async/await patterns
- Use parameter binding instead of code-behind logic

### Example - CORRECT ?
```razor
@page "/lists"
@inject ListStorageService ListService
@rendermode InteractiveWebAssembly

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="columns">
     <div class="column">
            <h1 class="title">My Lists</h1>
    @foreach (var list in lists)
   {
  <div class="box">
   <h2 class="subtitle">@list.Name</h2>
        <button class="button is-small" @onclick="() => DeleteList(list.Id)">
     Delete
   </button>
     </div>
      }
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private List<UserList> lists = new();
    
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
 lists = await ListService.GetAllListsAsync();
    }
    
    private async Task DeleteList(string id)
    {
        await ListService.DeleteListAsync(id);
        lists = await ListService.GetAllListsAsync();
    }
}
```

