## 10. Security

### Required Practices
- Never commit secrets (passwords, keys, connection strings)
- Always validate and sanitize user input
- Use parameterized queries (LINQ to MongoDB)
- Implement proper authentication on protected endpoints
- Use HTTPS in production
- Hash passwords with strong algorithms
- Validate JWT tokens on protected routes

### Example - CORRECT ?
```csharp
// Protected endpoint
[HttpGet]
[Authorize]
public async Task<ActionResult<UserList>> GetList(string id)
{
    var userId = User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
    var list = await _listService.GetListByIdAsync(id, userId);
    return Ok(list);
}
```

